 stops.\n\nThe shelves are cleared of bottled water in a few hours. The power's out, so boiling isn't an option. And the pumps and treatment plant that fill your glass all run on electricity.\n\nThe Blackout Survival Straw sits in a kitchen drawer until that day comes.\n\n✔️ 0.01 micron membrane stops bacteria and parasites\n✔️ Carbon stage for chemicals, sediment and taste\n✔️ 1,800 gallons from a single straw\n✔️ No batteries, no power, no parts to replace\n✔️ Stores 10+ years, ready when you need it\n\nOne per person. A 5-pack covers the whole house.\n\nIf you're a parent or grandparent, sort this before you need it, not during.\n\n👇 Get yours from the official site", "title": "Stop Storing Water. Make It Safe Instead. [47826]", "ctaText": "Learn more", "ctaType": "LEARN_MORE", "linkUrl": "https://www.tryblackoutwater.com/pages/advertorial", "linkDomain": "tryblackoutwater.com", "linkCaption": "www.tryblackoutwater.com", "linkDescription": "0.01 micron. 1,800 gallons. Carbon stage.", "displayFormat": "VIDEO", "imageUrls": [], "videoUrls": ["https://video.fgru6-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m366/AQM-32-lUE3cjIYjWDhYdAbsW9sdGZ4Xiy0aJ6lSocTOhq5_y8HfmnbPM1gj7BBLtHxFvqIrnq_JgiUoQ12TzzYFXe4TtCUAZ40PlM5u2R6USw.mp4?_nc_cat=105&_nc_oc=AdruJCCFnEcJ_uCwAtNrI0bP6VwVlQmwYho1TKKH9ka27mD1O47VUFTJhM5Iaqxho0y8WEXYO1_mI--iJ6SJUP8K&_nc_sid=b66105&_nc_ht=video.fgru6-1.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=CX_skGXvzkYQ7kNvwGZBWZX&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6Inhwdl9wcm9ncmVzc2l2ZS5WSV9VU0VDQVNFX1BST0RVQ1RfVFlQRS4uQzMuNzIwLmRhc2hfaDI2NC1iYXNpYy1nZW4yXzcyMHAiLCJ4cHZfYXNzZXRfaWQiOjMwNjMxNDQ2NDczNzI5NjQsImFzc2V0X2FnZV9kYXlzIjoxMSwidmlfdXNlY2FzZV9pZCI6MTAxMzksImR1cmF0aW9uX3MiOjE4MywidXJsZ2VuX3NvdXJjZSI6Ind3dyJ9&ccb=17-1&vs=64b31bbe8d32b0d1&_nc_&_nc_gid=r6Eild80jSH-nWa-pOaRSg&_nc_ss=7b289&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQRnRjkrFOd8C0jIQXWNSiLiwq2ZtBi_i1_1WD3jL0H6XA&oe=6B0085F7"], "videoPreviewUrls": ["https://scontent.fgru6-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t39.35426-6/890584305_1647851117010655_5661325164626317918_n.